        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The figures flanked a figure of the crucified Christ. They have been associated with the work of Neroccoi di Bartolommeo de'Landi (1447–1500), a Sienese painter and sculptor whose style fused the late Gothic with the early Renaissance."@en ;
